  "verbalization": "Zonisamide is likely to interact with Scn2b through a shared pathway involving voltage-gated sodium channels. The evidence suggests that Zonisamide binds to Scn11a and Scn4a, both of which participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, which in turn is participated by Scn2b. This indicates that Zonisamide may influence Scn2b through a common mechanism involving sodium channel activity. The high scores in both paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Zonisamide and Scn2b, likely mediated by their shared role in sodium channel function. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Zonisamide could modulate Scn2b, possibly through indirect effects on sodium channel activity.",
